Z||000000||86ttops||07-25-2001||03:14 PM||||I know this was just posted but I have a different kind of problem.  The belt feels plenty tight.  I just changed it with the Dayco brand a couple of days ago.  The bolt that screwed into the alternator on the bottom was broken off so I had to replace it with a new bolt.  First time around I used a bolt that i had laying around but the belt made noise right from the start so I tried tightening it again.  The second time I used a carriage bolt that fit into the slot so the bolt wouldn't turn and got it good and tight.  Now it squeals really load for awhile reving doesn't make it go away either.  When I went to work today it didn't go away until I got on the highway but it came back at idle in the parking lot.  I don't know what to do the belt has a little play but not very much at all.  The alternator is mounted straight before it looked crooked.  And this squeal is frickin load.  Any ideas? ||||reg||5
